        "tab_liquid_LDr3jc": {
          "type": "tab_liquid",
          "settings": {
            "title": "CARE INSTRUCTIONS",
            "custom_liquid": "{%- if product.type == 'Jewelry' -%}\n<p><style=\"text-align: center; color:#000000;\"><strong>Jewelry Care Instructions</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Keep jewelry away from water, moisture, and humidity. Avoid wearing it while swimming, bathing, or engaging in any water-related activities.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Store jewelry in a cool, dry place, preferably in a jewelry box or airtight container. This will prevent exposure to air, moisture, and dust, which can cause tarnishing and damage.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Avoid contact with perfumes, lotions, hairsprays, and other chemicals. These substances can react with the metal or stones in the jewelry and cause discoloration or deterioration.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Clean jewelry regularly using a soft cloth or a mild jewelry cleaner specifically designed for jewelry. Gently wipe the surface to remove any dirt, oils, or residue.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Handle the jewelry with care and avoid excessive pulling or tugging, as it can lead to the breakage of chains, clasps, or components.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>When not in use, store different pieces of jewelry separately to prevent scratching or tangling.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>If any stones become loose or fall out, get them repaired or replaced promptly to maintain the overall appearance and integrity of the jewelry.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Periodically inspect your jewelry for any signs of damage or wear. If you notice any issues, take it to a professional jeweler for repair.\n</li>\n</ul>\n{%-endif-%}\n{%- if product.type == 'Saree' or product.type == 'Blouse'-%}\n<p><style=\"text-align: center; color:#000000;\"><strong>Saree / Blouse Care Instructions</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Void washing silk sarees or blouses by hand or in a washing machine.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>If the saree/blouse becomes stained, promptly blot the stain with cold water.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Never dry silk/silk cotton sarees or blouses directly under sunlight as it can cause the color to fade.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Avoid bundling up the saree/blouse to prevent the zari/embroidery threads from tangling.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Store the saree/blouse in a breathable cotton muslin cloth, allowing air circulation and preventing sticking when stacked.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\n    <li>Do not store the saree/blouse in a plastic cover to avoid blackening of the gold zari.</li>\n</ul>\n{%-endif-%}\n{%- if product.type == 'Bag'-%}\n<p><style=\"text-align: center; color:#000000;\"><strong>Hand Bags Care Instructions</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Handle the handbag with clean hands to avoid transferring dirt, oils, or other substances onto the fabric or surface.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Protect the handbag from excessive moisture or water. Avoid using it in rainy conditions or placing it directly on wet surfaces.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>If the handbag gets stained, gently blot the stain with a clean cloth or sponge using mild soap and water. Avoid rubbing the stain vigorously, as it can damage the fabric or finish.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Avoid exposing the handbag to direct sunlight for prolonged periods, as it can cause fading or discoloration. When not in use, store the handbag in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Be cautious when handling sharp objects or rough surfaces to prevent scratches or tears on the handbag material.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; margin-bottom: auto;\">\n    <li>Avoid overstuffing the handbag, as it can distort the shape and strain the seams or handles. Instead, maintain a reasonable load to preserve the handbag&#39;s structural integrity.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\">\n    <li>Regularly clean the handbag&#39;s interior by emptying it and removing any debris or dust. Use a soft brush or a lint roller to gently clean the lining.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\">\n    <li>Store the handbag in a dust bag or a breathable cloth cover to protect it from dust, dirt, and potential scratches when not in use.</li>\n</ul>\n{%-endif-%}"
          }
        },
